        "consulted": "2026-11-14"
      }
    ],
    "en_301_549": {
      "numbering_rule": "In clause 9, the requirement for WCAG success criterion x.y.z is clause 9.x.y.z.",
      "where_the_standard_states_it": "EN 301 549 V4.1.1: each clause 9.x.y.z of clauses 9.1 to 9.4 requires the web page to satisfy the WCAG 2.2 success criterion x.y.z, which it names; clause 9.0 NOTE 5 says that void clauses are inserted to keep the numbering aligned with the WCAG 2.2 level A and AA success criteria. The standard has no separate correspondence table: the rule was checked clause by clause on the 55 non-void clauses.",
      "also_required": "Clause 9.6 (WCAG conformance requirements) and clause 9.7 (user preferences for web pages) have no WCAG success criterion number and are therefore not in `wcag`. See en-301-549.md.",
      "versions": {
        "V4.1.1": "Read in full for clauses 9.0 to 9.7 on the date above. All clause numbers in this file come from this version.",
        "V3.2.1": "Not read for this file. No clause number of V3.2.1 is given here.",
        "V2.1.2": "Not read. It is the version the RGAA 4.1.2 refers to."
      },
      "legal_status": "Which version carries a presumption of conformity is stated only in references/regulatory-status.md, section 1.2."
    },
    "official": [
      "rgaa.criteria[*].wcag and source_labels: copied from the official RGAA file; the labels are kept exactly as printed, including their differences of capitalisation.",
      "wcag[*].name and level: as printed in WCAG 2.2.",
      "wcag[*].en_301_549.V4.1.1: as read in the standard, one clause at a time."
    ],
    "not_official": [
      "wcag[*].rgaa is the reverse index of rgaa.criteria, computed by this project.",
      "Going from an RGAA criterion to an EN 301 549 clause through this file composes two official correspondences. No official table links RGAA 4.1.2 to EN 301 549 V4.1.1 or to WCAG 2.2 in the sources read: the official RGAA file targets WCAG 2.1.",
      "A WCAG success criterion listed for an RGAA criterion means that the official file relates the two. It does not mean that meeting the RGAA criterion is enough to satisfy the success criterion.",
      "For the six level A and AA success criteria added by WCAG 2.2, `rgaa` is null because the official RGAA 4.1.2 file does not list them. This file does not guess which RGAA criterion comes closest.",
      "WCAG techniques listed by the official RGAA file are not reproduced here; they are in the generated criteria files."
    ]
  },
